				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5214,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Fix search result handling with Mountain's response format\n\nSynchronize Element submodule with critical bug fixes:\n\n1. Sky: Fix text search result mapping to use Mountain's actual response format - `Hit.resource` instead of `Hit.uri`, and `Hit.matches[]` array (with `preview` and `line_number`) instead of flat hit shape. Add backwards-compat support for old flat `{uri, lineNumber, preview}` format.\n\n2. Sky: Fix search:findFiles IPC call to include required null exclude parameter. Previously MaxResults was shifted into wrong slot, causing glob extractor to ignore max and default to 10000. This resolves empty search results where previous code produced resource=MakeFileUri(\"\") with empty results array.\n\n3. Cocoon: Submodule sync to latest extension host changes.\n\nImpact: Text search and file search now return correct results using Mountain's response format, eliminating empty results from parameter order mismatch.",
			"SHA": "fe18d940fdbcd0272f2abe9a594c4b536121704b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T09:51:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5214,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Resolve URI object construction inconsistencies across editor services\n\nSubmodule synchronization completing the URI handling fix across multiple layers:\n1. Mountain: Use DebugOnce instead of dev_log! for unregistered view-action and workbench-internal commands to reduce log noise\n2. Output: Add missing URI class import to ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform, enabling SkyBridge to construct resource objects the workbench accepts directly\n3. Sky: Add BuildOpenArg helper that produces real URI instances when URI service is available, falling back to POJO only for code paths that call revive\n\nThis completes the fix from the previous commit for search results deduplication by ensuring open commands (vscode.open, OpenFile) also use proper URI construction rather than manual `{ $mid: 1, path, scheme }` objects that fail when consumers call uri.with() or uri.toString() directly.\n\nImpact: Consistent URI handling across search results and file open commands, eliminating \"uri.with is not a function\" errors and improving workbench result deduplication.",
			"SHA": "17f93c496ba1aac80c82c0e5cab95e4dc545d485"
		}
